  "scope": "D3D8 resolves 2D/cube/back-buffer resource, mip and face identity through its common surface locator. Bound cube parent refs are retained across caller release and released during rebind/reset/device-owned cleanup; current target size and CPU Clear mirror select the actual cube level. GetRenderTarget returns the matching cube parent/face/mip view. NULL color changes only depth and preserves the current color identity and viewport; missing depth queries return NOTFOUND and NULL. Larger depth extents are accepted and smaller ones refused against the current target even on depth-only calls. Explicit target changes reset the live viewport through an emitter shared with ordinary SetViewport, bypassing state-block recording for the target side effect; explicit SetViewport remains deferred. Validation precedes binding effects, while transport failures retain the existing accepted-prefix state policy. Native production functions cover all six faces/two levels, queries, sizes, validation, reference ordering, cleanup and recording boundaries. Real XP runs twelve colored cube passes through queried target views, depth-only switches, empty recorded blocks and an app-released held parent; the back buffer remains unchanged. Guest CPU replies are explicit simulations; separate actual GPU replay checks thirteen requests and 34816 pixels on both backends. Every oversized-depth pass clears depth first, so this does not validate preservation of prior depth data across target sizes. Source COM surface pointer identity, complete Reset resource boundaries, MSAA/depth type validation, duplicate MSAA creation (S2-43), wrapper conversion and stages 4/5/6 remain. No original Microsoft HAL or complete Wine/game/FPS result is claimed.",
